```json
{
  "eslint.validate": [
    "javascript",
    "javascriptreact",
    "typescript",
    "typescriptreact"
  ],
  "editor.formatOnSave": true,
  "editor.defaultFormatter": "esbenp.prettier-vscode"
}
```

### On Save Actions
- ESLint auto-fix runs on save
- Prettier formats code on save
- TypeScript checking for errors

## Best Practices

### ✅ DO
- Use explicit return types
- Define prop interfaces for all components
- Include all dependencies in useEffect
- Use const/let, not var
- Disable rules only with documented reasons
- Fix linting errors before committing
- Run `pnpm lint` in CI/CD pipelines

### ❌ DON'T
- Use `any` type
- Ignore ESLint errors
- Call hooks conditionally
- Commit console.log statements
- Disable rules globally
- Use default exports for components (export named)

